Fixes: 9bb7e0f24e7e ("cfg80211: add peer measurement with FTM initiator API")
Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>

Here is the root cause:
The bug is caused by a deadlock situation that occurs when the wireless device interface is destroyed while holding the `wdev->mtx` lock. The function `cfg80211_pmsr_wdev_down()` assumes that this lock is not held when it flushes the worker that requires the same lock, leading to a circular wait condition. The refactoring in the patch addresses this by directly processing the abort logic without scheduling a worker that could lead to deadlock.

